+# FrankenMoE roadmap — revision of 2026-09-06
+
+Audit: [docs/AUDIT-2026-09-06.md](docs/AUDIT-2026-09-06.md).
+Sequential task specification: [docs/QWEN-IMPLEMENTATION-TASK.md](docs/QWEN-IMPLEMENTATION-TASK.md).
+History: [experiments/EXPERIMENTS.md](experiments/EXPERIMENTS.md), individual EXP-028–033 cards and `benchmarks/history.jsonl`. Old decisions are preserved; a later clarification takes priority over the old "Next experiment".
+
+**The roadmap needs a substantial update.** The main goal is the patched expert-tier server. `bmoe-cli` remains a separate research branch. Their baselines, I/O and H2D must not be mixed. None of the queue below was implemented at audit time.
+
+## Phase status P0–P11
+
+| Phase | Current status and rationale |
+| --- | --- |
+| P0 — reproducibility | Partially done: EXP-000/004 and server measurements. Open: MTP provenance, artifact preservation, a unified profile and async transfer correctness. |
+| P1 — SSD/RAM/GPU | Old CPU-decode prefetch options are closed: EXP-001/002/003/012/025/027. Bulk CUDA prefill is open separately per EXP-030/031/032. EXP-033 single-buffer packed staging was rejected. |
+| P2 — hot cache | Basic RAM LRU and VRAM banks exist in bmoe-cli; server-side EHS activation was rejected by EXP-010. No new cache is planned without reuse/memory evidence. |
+| P3 — router prefetch | Late madvise and the warmer were rejected. The next layer's router is still unknown. Only provable intra-layer overlap can become a separate experiment; route prediction is deferred. |
+| P4 — container/reads | Addressable split-GGUF/O_DIRECT already exists in bmoe-cli. Model repacking and a new I/O engine are deferred. Exact merging of adjacent H2D expert ranges already exists in the server scheduler. |
+| P5 — kernels | EXP-019 micro-tuning is closed at the current priority, EXP-021 microbench was done, EXP-028 CPU fused integration was rejected. Bulk prefill is actually CUDA MMQ; a CPU fused retry is not planned. |
+| P6 — speculative | EXP-022 ngram and EXP-023 CPU-only draft were rejected; EXP-024 split MTP was accepted historically (+13.6%, one pair). Patch deliverability and broader correctness are not yet confirmed. `n_max=2`; do not retry a larger limit. |
+| P7 — memory planning | The RAM startup gate and EHS safe autofit were implemented in EXP-008/009; a full planner is deferred. Open: validation of the active watchdog/launch profile. |
+| P8 — mixed quant | Deferred: no representative quality baseline or quality budget. |
+| P9 — REAP | Deferred for the same reason; do not change the model or top-k. |
+| P10 — batching | Deferred until the single-request path is stable and lifetime is verified with several requests. Aggregate tok/s is a separate metric. |
+| P11 — API/autotuning | The OpenAI-compatible server already works. Autotuning and UI are not the next step. |
+
+## Execution queue
+
+The IDs below reserve the meaning of the stages; an EXP date is assigned at start. Do not present them as completed experiments.
+
+1. **R0 / EXP-034 — provenance and a reproducible package**. Record the state of the root/nested trees, the MTP diff, sources/libraries/commands and the surviving data. In an isolated copy prepare a minimal reproducible MTP patch; do not update upstream and do not touch the integration tree. Gate: the required configuration is reproducible, missing data is explicitly marked.
+2. **R1 / EXP-035 — a working safety profile**. A separate correctness stage: external watchdog units, enabling the internal watchdog in an explicit benchmark profile, correct monitor termination. Do not provoke real swap/OOM. Gate: synthetic thresholds/lifecycle, then an unchanged inference configuration.
+3. **R2 / EXP-036 — an up-to-date baseline and correctness fixtures**. One chosen 32K MTP profile, `n_max=2`, EHS=0, 12 threads. Fixed requests, full prefill without prompt-cache reuse, a separate warm decode, unified raw artifacts. This is the baseline for new work, not a repeat of the MTP/no-MTP contest.
+4. **R3 / EXP-037 — offline transfer budget and dependency map**. Use the already saved EXP-031/032 first. Split GPU H2D duration, host API time, syncs and gaps; verify the request span and free staging slot availability. Do not re-capture the already known 22.16 GiB expert attribution.
+5. **R4 / EXP-038 — conditional bounded pinned ring without packing/scatter**. Only if R3 shows a measurable host-side submission bottleneck and the possibility of preparing the next chunk. Two bounded host slots, direct copies into the original offsets, the same CUDA stream. This is a CPU-staging/H2D overlap hypothesis; true H2D/compute overlap is not promised. With an insufficient expected effect — `NOT_RUN`, move to conditional R5 or finish P1.
+6. **R5 / EXP-039 — conditional intra-layer transfer/compute overlap**. Only with new dependency/timeline evidence after R3/R4. A separate copy stream, readiness/last-consumer events, bounded extra memory. Do not present a pointer to a scheduler buffer as a lifetime guarantee. If no safe independent window exists — `NOT_RUN`, direction `DEFERRED`.
+7. **R6 — acceptance of the concrete winner**. A representative short/main/long prompt, decode, repeated requests, cancellation/checkpoint/shutdown. Only then the delivery patch and a default-change proposal. No winner — keep the baseline and finish with a negative result.
+
+If R4 is accepted, R6 comes first. R5 starts as a separate cycle only after the handoff and only with a remaining measured bottleneck. R4 and R5 are not implemented simultaneously.
+
+## Decision rule
+
+One experiment, one hypothesis, one baseline, one primary variable. Performance ACCEPTED requires a ≥3% median prefill-time reduction, confirmation by paired results outside the observed noise, and no unacceptable regressions. Fewer H2D calls, working code or less CPU spin are not success by themselves. At least five consecutive pairs for acceptance; early rejection on clear failure is allowed. Correctness/infrastructure experiments are accepted by their own pre-declared functional criteria without a speed claim.
+
+Keep a bad result in the journal, do not include the code. `INCONCLUSIVE`, `BLOCKED`, `NOT_RUN` must not turn into ACCEPTED. A handoff is mandatory after every stage, including rejection and blocking. Model runs and commits are governed by [agents.md](agents.md); the audit is not permission to run.
+
+## Old roadmap (historical pre-audit snapshot)
+
+P0 was marked done; P1: SSD→RAM→GPU overlap, aligned/coalesced reads, pinned RAM, double/triple buffering; P2: hot cache; P3: router prefetch; P4: addressed aligned container; P5: fused dequant+GEMM Ada/decode; P6: MTP/ngram/draft/combined; P7: residency planner; P8: mixed quant; P9: REAP; P10: multi-agent batching; P11: autotuning/API. All of P1–P11 had unchecked boxes. The critical path was formulated as P0 → true H2D/compute overlap. That order is replaced by the R0–R6 queue above; the experimental history is not deleted.
